From d2a6cf66378f694e4c243cfa77d6b200b4e4c009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:20:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] rk3576_u: drop the uhf_device file_contexts entry - it
 collides with the platform's own usb_serial_device label

Real build failure, found by actually running the build (not by
inspection):

  file_contexts.concat.tmp: Multiple different specifications for
  /dev/ttyUSB[0-9]*  (u:object_r:uhf_device:s0 and
  u:object_r:usb_serial_device:s0).
  Error: could not load context file from file_contexts.concat.tmp

system/sepolicy/private/file_contexts has labeled /dev/ttyUSB[0-9]*
usb_serial_device platform-wide since sepolicy API 30 - this file's own
device-specific uhf_device override for the exact same pattern is a hard
conflict, not a precedence question; sefcontext_compile refuses to guess
which one wins.

Removed the override. The companion commit in hardware/rockchip/uhf
(hal_uhf.te) grants hal_uhf_default access to the platform's own
usb_serial_device type directly instead of a bespoke uhf_device one, so
NFR-S-01 (only the HAL domain touches the reader's device node) still
holds - confirmed no other domain on this product is granted
usb_serial_device access. The OI-05 TODO about narrowing past every
ttyUSB* once the reader's real VID/PID is confirmed is unchanged by this
- it was already the same "every ttyUSB* on the board" approximation
either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rk3576_u/sepolicy/file_contexts | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rk3576_u/sepolicy/file_contexts b/rk3576_u/sepolicy/file_contexts
index 10866e3..4b1e718 100644
--- a/rk3576_u/sepolicy/file_contexts
+++ b/rk3576_u/sepolicy/file_contexts
@@ -1,7 +1,12 @@
 # UHF-SRS-001 NFR-S-01. Board-specific: this reader enumerates as /dev/ttyUSB0 on rk3576_u.
-# uhf_device is declared once, board-independently, in
-# hardware/rockchip/uhf/aidl/default/sepolicy/hal_uhf.te.
+#
+# No file_contexts entry here (deliberately, not an oversight): system/sepolicy/private/
+# file_contexts already labels /dev/ttyUSB[0-9]* usb_serial_device platform-wide, and
+# sefcontext_compile rejects a second, different label for the same exact pattern - confirmed by
+# actually hitting that build error with an earlier uhf_device override this file used to carry.
+# hal_uhf.te (hardware/rockchip/uhf/aidl/default/sepolicy) grants hal_uhf_default access to
+# usb_serial_device directly instead.
 #
 # TODO(OI-05): narrow past every ttyUSB* once R1 confirms this reader's USB vendor/product ID —
-# mirrors the same open item on this product's ueventd.uhf.rc DAC rule.
-/dev/ttyUSB[0-9]*   u:object_r:uhf_device:s0
+# mirrors the same open item on this product's ueventd.uhf.rc DAC rule. When that lands, it'll
+# need a real per-path or by-id label distinct from usb_serial_device, added back here.
